{
  "_comment": [
    "Tolerances for the genuine-mesh-change steps, compared against a stored",
    "reference.json. Unlike the identity check there is no analytic invariant to",
    "assert here: interpolating onto a different mesh changes the field, and the",
    "20 steps that follow are a smoke test that the remapped state is a valid",
    "initial condition (finite, divergence-free after projection, mass-consistent)",
    "rather than a statement about the physics.",
    "",
    "Values therefore match tests/tools/tolerances.json, which is calibrated to",
    "survive decomposition and compiler changes while still catching a real",
    "regression in the remap path by orders of magnitude.",
    "",
    "The Poisson and mass-conservation residuals are absolute-only: they are",
    "round-off quantities whose reproducible content is their magnitude."
  ],

